[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: TC-H1FWT-
TITLE: Test Protocol

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-15
TITLE: Timer Characteristics 1 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user runs a treatment plan for 121 seconds, make sure the timers can handle 
the timing of 2 minutes without any issues even though with a special version of firmware 
application that doesn’t stop the treatment.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* A treatment plan is loaded and ready for run about 2 minutes 
* The system is ready to run without any issues. 
* Load a firmware application that doesn’t stop the treatment.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start a run for the loaded treatment plan for 121 seconds.
2. Check the timers on GUI
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started without any issues. 
2. Verify the timers can handle about 2 minutes treatment without any issues.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWT-10
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-16
TITLE: Timer Functionality 1 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
If a user reset the timers in the middle of emission, verify the emission finishes as normal and basically resetting the timers doesn’t effect on emission. Also, the timers won’t count down.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to use and run a loaded treatment plan
* A treatment plan is loaded into the system.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run a normal treatment of 20 seconds
2. After 5 seconds of emission, reset the timers through the screen by clicking reset timer button.
3. Check the ongoing emission process
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started
2. Verify the timers are resetting
3. Verify that the emission finishes as normal without the timers resetting. Also, the timers won’t countdown if the system is running.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWT-3
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-17
TITLE: Timer Functionality 2 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When the system starts and finishes an emission, resetting the timers will set the timers to 0
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* A treatment plan is loaded and ready for run
* The system is ready to run without any issues.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run a normal treatment of 20 seconds
2. Wait till the emission is done without any issues.
3. Click the Reset Timer button
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started
2. Verify the system’s state went back to ready. Also, verify that the timer values are within 20 seconds +/- 10%.
3. Verify that the timers reset, and their values are 0
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWT-2
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-18
TITLE: Communication 1 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
If a special version of the firmware application loads into Mainboard where the treatment won’t stop. The treatment can’t run because of the interlocks’ fault.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* A treatment plan is loaded and ready for run
* The system is ready to run without any issues.
* Load a special version of Firmware application where won’t stop the treatment.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run a normal treatment of 20 seconds
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission can’t start because of the un-cleared interlock’s fault.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWT-6
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-19
TITLE: Communication 2 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When a user starts an emission, the timers will start to increase.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* A treatment plan is loaded and ready for run
* The system is ready to run without any issues.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run a normal treatment of 20 seconds
2. Check the timers at the top of the GUI
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started
2. Verify the timers started to increase
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWT-6
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-20
TITLE: Timer Functionality 4 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
If a special version of the firmware application loads into Mainboard where the treatment won’t stop, the backup timers will stop the emission. Also, the interlocks’ fault won’t clear and remains even after 10 minutes.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* A treatment plan is loaded and ready for run
* The system is ready to run without any issues.
* Load a special version of Firmware application where the timers won’t stop the treatment.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run a normal treatment of 20 seconds
2. After 20 seconds, check the emission.
3. Wait for at least 10 minutes
4. Check the interlock faults
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started
2. Verify the emission stopped at 20 seconds +/- 10% because of the back timers even though the main timers won’t let the emission stop.
3. Verify 10 minutes passed.
4. Verify the faults still remains
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-22
TITLE: Timer Characteristics 2 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When user has started to run a normal 20 second treatment plan, make sure the timers’ values increased and have a reported resolution of 0.01 seconds.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* A treatment plan is loaded and ready for run about 20 seconds
* The system is ready to run without any issues.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start a run for the loaded treatment plan for 20 seconds.
2. Check the timers on GUI
3. Check timeout counter
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started without any issues
2. Verify the timers’ values increased and have a reported resolution of 0.01 seconds
3. Verify it has a minimum resolution of 60 milliseconds or less.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWT-11
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-23
TITLE: Timer Functionality 5 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When a treatment plan started to run by user, the timers increase accordingly.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* A treatment plan is loaded and ready for run
* The system is ready to run without any issues.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run a normal treatment of 20 seconds
2. Check the timers
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started
2. Verify the timers increase during emission
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-24
TITLE: Timer Functionality 6 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The timers won’t increase when the emission stops.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* A treatment plan is loaded and ready for run
* The system is ready to run without any issues.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run a normal treatment of 20 seconds
2. After 5 seconds, stop through GUI by clicking the STOP button.
3. Check the timers
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started
2. Verify the emission stopped
3. Verify the timers won’t increase and stops counting
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-25
TITLE: Timer Functionality 7 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When a user starts to run a treatment plan, verify backup timers can terminate the emission accordingly.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* A treatment plan is loaded and ready for run
* The system is ready to run without any issues.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run a normal treatment of 20 seconds
2. After 20 seconds, check the emission.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started
2. Verify the emission stopped at 20 seconds +/- 10% because of the backup timers.
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-26
TITLE: Timer Functionality 3 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
If a special version of the firmware application loads into Mainboard where the treatment won’t stop, the backup timers will stop the emission. Also, the interlocks’ fault won’t clear and remains till the timers resetting time.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* A treatment plan is loaded and ready for run
* The system is ready to run without any issues.
* Load a special version of Firmware application where the timers won’t stop the treatment.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run a normal treatment of 20 seconds
2. Wait till the emission is done after 20 seconds.
3. Wait at least 1 minute and check the faults
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started
2. Verify the system’s state went back to ready. Also, verify that the backup timers stopped the emission after 20 seconds despite of the non-stopping timer version of the firmware.
3. Verify that the interlock’s faults are not cleared
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWT-27
TITLE: Timer Characteristics 3 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When a user starts to run the loaded treatment plan, it shouldn’t stop the treatment because of the special version of the firmware application.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* Specific version of firmware application is loaded which its main timer doesn’t stop the treatment.
* The system is ready to use and run a loaded treatment plan
* A treatment plan is loaded into the system.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Run the loaded treatment plan using a point of duration 20 seconds.
2. Wait for at least 1 minute without clearing errors or resetting timers.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the emission started. Also, verify that the backup timers terminate the emission at 20 seconds +/- 10%
2. Verify that the timers’ values on the screen do not continue to count
<<<

